WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.691
An empirical study passes every condition

00:00:03.711 --> 00:00:05.675
in a carefully built search.

00:00:05.824 --> 00:00:07.866
It concerns the right service, the right

00:00:07.886 --> 00:00:09.850
setting and the right dates.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.809
Have we established that it answers the

00:00:11.829 --> 00:00:12.853
reader's question?

00:00:13.015 --> 00:00:13.896
Take a moment.

00:00:16.305 --> 00:00:18.420
We have established a useful match.

00:00:18.582 --> 00:00:19.657
Whether it helps depends on what the

00:00:19.677 --> 00:00:21.744
reader is trying to accomplish.

00:00:21.894 --> 00:00:24.632
Relevance is a relationship: relevant to

00:00:24.652 --> 00:00:26.422
someone, for something.

00:00:27.345 --> 00:00:29.910
The information need is the fuller purpose

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:31.134
behind a search.

00:00:31.296 --> 00:00:34.562
Queries, filters and task briefs can

00:00:34.582 --> 00:00:37.023
communicate substantial detail about it.

00:00:37.185 --> 00:00:39.897
A query represents that need; it is not

00:00:39.917 --> 00:00:41.211
the need itself.

00:00:41.799 --> 00:00:44.356
Follow the chain: information need,

00:00:44.376 --> 00:00:47.140
representation, retrieval signals,

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:49.678
retrieved records, human judgement.

00:00:49.853 --> 00:00:51.779
The system works directly with the middle

00:00:51.799 --> 00:00:54.898
three. Detailed requests and feedback can

00:00:54.918 --> 00:00:56.791
help it estimate suitability.

00:00:56.954 --> 00:00:59.420
The reader still assesses usefulness.

00:01:00.342 --> 00:01:02.738
The chapter's hypothetical librarian wants

00:01:02.758 --> 00:01:05.612
recent empirical studies of generative AI

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:08.963
services for research support in academic

00:01:08.983 --> 00:01:11.398
libraries. The strategy combines

00:01:11.418 --> 00:01:14.762
alternatives: generative AI or large

00:01:14.782 --> 00:01:17.390
language models; academic library or

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:20.200
university library; research support or

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:21.707
research consultation.

00:01:22.272 --> 00:01:24.551
Publication dates are limited to twenty

00:01:24.571 --> 00:01:25.981
twenty-four onwards.

00:01:26.156 --> 00:01:28.713
These explicit conditions communicate much

00:01:28.733 --> 00:01:31.239
more than a handful of broad keywords.

00:01:31.401 --> 00:01:34.177
Now keep the resulting study fixed while

00:01:34.197 --> 00:01:35.826
we change the purpose.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:38.690
The invented study reports positive

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:41.074
participant reactions after a short

00:01:41.094 --> 00:01:43.754
demonstration of a university library's

00:01:43.774 --> 00:01:46.640
generative AI research-support service.

00:01:46.816 --> 00:01:48.896
It matches the search and is topically

00:01:48.916 --> 00:01:51.692
suitable. For an introductory workshop, it

00:01:51.712 --> 00:01:54.386
provides a useful example of a service and

00:01:54.406 --> 00:01:56.125
participants' responses.

00:01:56.679 --> 00:01:58.837
For a service-adoption decision, those

00:01:58.857 --> 00:02:00.782
reactions are insufficient.

00:02:00.919 --> 00:02:03.591
They do not establish answer accuracy,

00:02:03.625 --> 00:02:06.414
staff workload or performance in real

00:02:06.434 --> 00:02:09.442
consultations. The study still contributes

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:11.413
evidence about reactions.

00:02:11.576 --> 00:02:14.042
Its contribution changes with the purpose;

00:02:14.218 --> 00:02:16.349
its search match has not changed.

00:02:17.253 --> 00:02:19.594
Targeted follow-up searches can seek

00:02:19.614 --> 00:02:22.648
accuracy evaluations, workload evidence

00:02:22.668 --> 00:02:24.090
and real-world use.

00:02:24.253 --> 00:02:26.630
Then inspect what each study measured,

00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:28.073
under what conditions, and whether the

00:02:28.093 --> 00:02:29.954
findings support the decision.

00:02:30.512 --> 00:02:32.810
Making every issue a compulsory search

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:35.683
condition can also miss useful studies.

00:02:35.858 --> 00:02:38.505
They may use unexpected terminology or

00:02:38.525 --> 00:02:41.353
report the issue only in full text.

00:02:41.515 --> 00:02:43.956
Better searching and relevance judgement

00:02:43.976 --> 00:02:45.013
work together.

00:02:45.903 --> 00:02:48.612
Evidence-synthesis searchers call some of

00:02:48.632 --> 00:02:51.099
these search-resistant concepts.

00:02:51.261 --> 00:02:54.642
A review criterion may be poorly indexed,

00:02:54.805 --> 00:02:57.336
inconsistently described or difficult to

00:02:57.356 --> 00:03:00.119
express as dependable search terms.

00:03:00.657 --> 00:03:03.272
A strategy may retrieve a broader set of

00:03:03.292 --> 00:03:05.527
potentially relevant records and leave

00:03:05.547 --> 00:03:07.614
some criteria to screening.

00:03:07.776 --> 00:03:09.741
This is a deliberate division of work

00:03:09.761 --> 00:03:12.085
between retrieval and assessment.

00:03:12.235 --> 00:03:14.638
It does not make searching or eligibility

00:03:14.658 --> 00:03:16.274
criteria unimportant.

00:03:17.179 --> 00:03:19.484
Relevance can concern a system's estimated

00:03:19.504 --> 00:03:22.667
match, topical suitability, a contribution

00:03:22.687 --> 00:03:24.613
to the reader's understanding, or

00:03:24.633 --> 00:03:26.198
usefulness for a task.

00:03:26.373 --> 00:03:28.763
These are related perspectives, with no

00:03:28.783 --> 00:03:30.553
single hierarchy among them.

00:03:31.125 --> 00:03:34.074
Boolean matching, BM twenty-five,

00:03:34.108 --> 00:03:36.227
embeddings and neural rerankers help

00:03:36.247 --> 00:03:37.592
estimate relevance.

00:03:37.768 --> 00:03:39.784
A high score cannot turn participant

00:03:39.804 --> 00:03:42.503
reactions into evidence of answer

00:03:42.523 --> 00:03:45.273
accuracy. Ask what the record contributes

00:03:45.293 --> 00:03:46.884
to this reader's purpose.
